    5                /       LAST EDIT: 22-MAY-2014 CJL.
    6   
    7                /       TAKEN FROM A 1978 P?S/8 SYSTEM TAPE IMAGE [KNOWN TO NOT BE A FINAL RELEASE].
    8   
    9                /       THIS IS THE ACTUAL IMAGE OF BLOCK 0060 OF A P?S/8 SYSTEM TAPE.  BLOCK 0060 IS
   10                /       RESERVED AS THE "FILE" TO BE PASSED TO THE SLURP LOADER LAST IF THE /I SWITCH
   11                /       IS PASSED TO THE "BIN" UTILITY WHEN INVOKED TO LOAD BINARY FILES.
   12   
   13                /       SUCCESSFUL OPERATION DEPENDS ON THIS "FILE" BEING THE LAST FILE DESCRIPTOR IN
   14                /       THE FILE LIST.  MOST OF THE CODING IS LOADED OVER THE SYSTEM FILE AREA
   15                /       [07757-07777] SINCE AT THE POINT THIS "FILE" BEING LOADED, THE FORMER CONTENTS
   16                /       OF ARE MEANINGLESS.  ONCE THE CODE IS COMPLETELY LOADED, THE SLURP LOADER IS
   17                /       OVERLAID TO PASS CONTROL TO THE JUST-LOADED CODE.
   18   
   19                /       THE TC01/TC08 DECTAPE SYSTEM HANDLER IS OPERATIONAL IF ALL ADDRESSES FROM
   20                /       SBOOT [7600] THROUGH SADDR [7746] ARE LOADED.  THE REST OF THE PAGE NEED NOT
   21                /       BE LOADED FOR THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER TO COMPLETELY FUNCTION; SYSTEM RESTART
   22                /       AT 07600 WILL BE OPERATIONAL.
   23   
   24                /       MORE IMPORTANTLY, BY AVOIDING OVERLAYING THE REST OF THE PAGE, THE CODE IN
   25                /       CONTROL IS NOT OVERLAID.  THE ORIGINAL STARTUP INFORMATION PASSED TO THE SLURP
   26                /       LOADER IS ALSO INTACT ALLOWING STARTUP AT THE INTENDED ADDRESS AND FIELD.
   27   
   28                /       TO END THE TAPE OPERATION RELOADING THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER FROM BLOCK 0000,
   29                /       REFERENCE CAN BE MADE TO VARIOUS CONSTANTS WITHIN THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.
   30                /       A CONSTANT 0200 IS REQUIRED TO STOP THE TAPE; IT IS AVAILABLE WITHIN THE
   31                /       SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER CODE JUST READ IN.
   32   
   33                /       OPERATIONAL CHANGES DUE TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER OVERLAYING THE SLURP
   34                /       LOADER.
   35   
   36                /       THE ONLY INTERNAL CHANGE IS THE EXACT VALUE OF THE DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS
   37                /       USED WHEN NONE IS SPECIFIED ON THE COMMAND-LINE.  A NEW SAFE HALT DEFAULT
   38                /       LOCATION IS DEFINED WITHIN THE CODE READ INTO THE SYSTEM FILE AREA.
   39                /       ADDITIONALLY, A JMP BACK TO THE SAFE HALT IS INCLUDED IN CASE THE USER PRESSES
   40                /       "CONTINUE" ON THE FRONT PANEL OF THE CPU.  THE "BIN" UTILITY CHANGES THE
   41                /       DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS FROM THAT OF THE SLURP LOADER TO THE SAFE HALT
   42                /       ADDRESS DEFINED HERE; ONCE-ONLY INITIALIZATION OF THE "BIN" UTILITY HANDLES
   43                /       ALL CASES.
   44   
   45                /       WHEN THE USER PROGRAM IS LOADED AND STARTED, THE NET EFFECT IS THAT THE SYSTEM
   46                /       DEVICE HANDLER IS ALSO RESIDENT IN MEMORY.  THE EQUIVALENT RESULTS WOULD HAVE
   47                /       BEEN ACHIEVED USING THE VIRTUAL LOADER; HOWEVER, THE OVERHEAD OF THE VIRTUAL
   48                /       LOADER HAS BEEN ELIMINATED.  THE LOADING PROCESS IS NOTICEABLY FASTER; THE
   49                /       SYSTEM DEVICE CAN REMAIN WRITE-LOCKED UNLESS THE USER PROGRAM REQUIRES ACCESS
   50                /       TO WRITE OPERATIONS OF THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.  [NOTE: THE SYSTEM DEVICE
   51                /       HANDLER RECOVERS FROM ANY DEVICE ERROR.  AS SUCH, THE USER CAN ENABLE WRITING
   52                /       LATER, WHERE APPROPRIATE, TO HARMLESSLY RECOVER FROM ANY FORM OF SYSTEM DEVICE
   53                /       ERROR SUCH AS WRITE-LOCK.]


/    SYSTEM HANDLER RELOAD ROUTINE   P?S PAL V08I    22-MAY-14  PAGE 2

   55                /       THE "GET" COMMAND CAN USE EITHER THE OVERALL METHOD DESCRIBED HERE OR SPECIFY
   56                /       THE /V OPTION TO INVOKE THE VIRTUAL LOADER.  THE PERMANENT CONTENTS OF BLOCK
   57                /       0000 ARE IDENTICAL TO WHAT THE VIRTUAL LOADER SETS UP IN THE SYSTEM LOADER
   58                /       AREA [TO SAVE ALL USER MEMORY AND THEN RESTART THE SYSTEM].  [NOTE: THE
   59                /       INTERNAL OPERATIONS OF THE VIRTUAL LOADER INCLUDE CALLS PLACED IN THE SYSTEM
   60                /       LOADER REPLACING THE DEFAULT VALUES.  SINCE THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER IS NEVER
   61                /       DISPLACED WHEN THE VIRTUAL LOADER IS IN EFFECT, ONE OF THE LAST ACTIONS OF THE
   62                /       VIRTUAL LOADER IS TO RESTORE THE SYSTEM LOADER TO ITS DEFAULT CONTENTS.]  THIS
   63                /       ENSURES THAT STARTING THE PROGRAM AT 07632 WILL PERFORM THE MEMORY SAVE
   64                /       OPERATION AND THEN RESTART THE SYSTEM.  [NOTE: "GET" IS ACTUALLY AN ALTERNATE
   65                /       ENTRY INTO THE "BIN" PROGRAM THAT FORCES APPROPRIATE COMMAND-LINE SWITCHES;
   66                /       "BIN" CAN BE INVOKED WITH THE IDENTICAL OPTIONS EXPLICITLY GIVEN; HOWEVER,
   67                /       THESE OPTIONS ARE NOT FORCES AS IN THE "GET" COMMAND.]
   68   
   69                /       WHEN THE /I SWITCH IS GIVEN CAUSING THE LOADING OF THIS "FILE", THE OVERALL
   70                /       MAXIMUM USER-SPECIFIED FILE COUNT DROPS FROM SEVENTEEN TO SIXTEEN.
   71   
   72                /       KNOWN LIMITATIONS.
   73   
   74                /       THE ONCE-ONLY CODE OF THE "BIN" UTILITY REQUIRES SOME REWORK TO PREVENT
   75                /       ATTEMPTS AT IMPOSSIBLE COMMANDS.  IF THE /I SWITCH IS GIVEN, AN ERROR MESSAGE
   76                /       SHOULD BE ISSUED IF EXACTLY SEVENTEEN FILES ARE SUPPLIED BY THE USER.
   77                /       PRESENTLY, IN THE SPECIFIC RELEASE REFERENCED, THE SEVENTEENTH FILE IS MERELY
   78                /       IGNORED.  THIS CAN EASILY BE CORRECTED IN A FUTURE RELEASE OF EITHER P?S/8 OR
   79                /       THE "BIN" UTILITY.
   80   
   81                /       THIS VERSION OF THE /I "FILE" DOES NOT SUPPORT MULTIPLE LOGICAL UNITS FOR THE
   82                /       SYSTEM DEVICE.  THE TC01/TC08 CAN SUPPORT A SPECIAL SUPERSET BOOTSTRAP ROUTINE
   83                /       TO ALLOW BOOTUP TO A SYSTEM ON A LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT OTHER THAN 0.  THIS CODE
   84                /       MUST BE UPGRADED TO MAINTAIN FULL COMPATIBILITY.
   85   
   86                /       TO ACCOMPLISH THIS, THE CODE CAN BE REWORKED TO OVERLAY ADDITIONAL AREAS OF
   87                /       THE SLURP LOADER THAT CAN BE DESTROYED WHILE THE LOADING OF THIS CODE IS IN
   88                /       EFFECT.  FOR EXAMPLE, THIS CODE IS TOTALLY LOCATED WITHIN A SINGLE DECTAPE
   89                /       BLOCK.  PART OF THE SLURP LOADER CODING IS CONCERNED WITH ADDITIONAL BLOCK
   90                /       TRANSFERS; A TYPICAL BINARY TFS FILE CONTAINS UP TO SIXTEEN BLOCKS.  SUCH
   91                /       SECTIONS OF CODE ARE NO LONGER NEEDED WHEN THIS CODE IS IN CONTROL.  THUS,
   92                /       SOME ADDITIONAL WORDS OF THIS "FILE" CODE MIGHT BE LOCATED OVER THE STATED 
   93                /       PORTION OF THE [NO LONGER NEEDED] SLURP LOADER CODING.
   94   
   95                /       PORTIONS OF THE BOOTSTRAP CODE WITHIN THE SLURP LOADER ARE USED BY THIS CODE;
   96                /       HOWEVER, MUCH OF IT IS NOT; THIS WOULD ALSO ALLOW POTENTIAL LENGTHENING OF
   97                /       THIS "FILE" TO ACCOMMODATE ADDITIONAL FEATURES.


/    SYSTEM HANDLER RELOAD ROUTINE   P?S PAL V08I    22-MAY-14  PAGE 3

   99                /       DEFINED SYMBOLS.
  100   
  101                /       NOTE: OTHER THAN THE SLURP CONTROL DEFINITIONS, THE REST OF THE DEFINITIONS ON
  102                /       THIS PAGE HAVE BEEN TAKEN FROM OTHER P?S/8 SOURCE FILES TO ALLOW THIS CODE TO
  103                /       BE ASSEMBLED AS AN INDEPENDENT SOURCE CODE FILE.  GENERALLY ALL COMPONENTS OF
  104                /       THE TC01/TC08 OVERALL SUPPORT ARE COMBINED TOGETHER WHEN P?S/8 IS BEING
  105                /       CREATED.
  106   
  107                /       P?S/8 SYSTEM DEFINITIONS.
  108   
  109          7600          SBOOT=  7600                    /SYSTEM REBOOT ADDRESS
  110          7757          SFILES= 7757                    /PASSED FILE LIST STARTS HERE
  111          7632          SLOAD=  7632                    /SYSTEM LOADER ADDRESS
  112   
  113                /       P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER DEFINITIONS.
  114   
  115          7602          S200=   7602                    /CONSTANT 0200
  116          7746          SADDR=  7746                    /LATEST TRANSFER ADDRESS
  117   
  118                /       SLURP LOADER DEFINITIONS.
  119   
  120          7626          SLPSTRT=7626                    /SLURP LOADER NEXT FILE ADDRESS
  121          7746          SLUSTRT=7746                    /SLURP LOADER PROGRAM START ADDRESS
  122          7613          SLWAIT= 7613                    /SLURP BOOTSTRAP WAIT ROUTINE
  123          7637          SL220=  7637                    /CONSTANT 0220
  124          7607          SL600=  7607                    /CONSTANT 0600
  125          7623          SL7577= 7623                    /CONSTANT 7577
  126   
  127                /       SLURP CONTROL DEFINITIONS.
  128          0000          DA=     0                       /DATA WORD      
  129          0001          EF=     1                       /END-OF-FILE
  130          0003          FL=     3                       /FIELD SETTING
  131          0002          OR=     2                       /ORIGIN SETTING
  132   
  133                /       TC01/TC08 DECTAPE DEFINITIONS.
  134   
  135          7755          CA=     7755                    /CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER FOR 3-CYCLE DATA BREAK
  136          6762          DTCA=   6762                    /CLEAR STATUS REGISTER "A"
  137          6766          DTLA=   6766                    /LOAD STATUS REGISTER "A" FROM AC, CLEAR AC
  138          6774          DTLB=   6774                    /AC[6-8] TO BREAK FIELD, CLEAR AC
  139          6761          DTRA=   6761                    /STATUS REGISTER "A" .OR. INTO AC
  140          6772          DTRB=   6772                    /STATUS REGISTER "B" .OR. INTO AC
  141          6771          DTSF=   6771                    /SKIP ON DECTAPE FLAG OR ERROR FLAG SET
  142          6764          DTXA=   6764                    /AC .XOR. INTO STATUS REGISTER "A", CLEAR AC
  143          7754          WC=     7754                    /WORD COUNT REGISTER FOR 3-CYCLE DATA BREAK


/    SYSTEM HANDLER RELOAD ROUTINE   P?S PAL V08I    22-MAY-14  PAGE 4

  145                /       THE "FILE" IMAGE REQUIRES AN AVAILABLE BUFFER WHEN THE SYSTEM IS BEING
  146                /       CREATED.
  147   
  148                /       SINCE IT IS READ IN ONE WORD AT A TIME BY THE SLURP LOADER, THE INTERNAL
  149                /       ORIGIN WILL BE SET ACCORDINGLY FOR ASSEMBLY PURPOSES.  THE BUFFER ADDRESS IS
  150                /       ONLY USED WHEN THE SYSTEM IS GENERATED [OR SOME EQUIVALENT SYSTEM
  151                /       RECONFIGURATION UTILITY EVENTUALLY WRITTEN TO SIMPLIFY THE PROCESS].
  152   
  153         *7200          *7200                           /BUFFER ADDRESS FOR SYSTEM GENERATION PURPOSES.
  154   
  155         *7600          RELOC   SBOOT                   /PAGE WHERE EVERYTHING HAPPENS.
  156   
  157                /       NOTE: THIS IS AN IMAGE OF A VALID [SHORT] SLURP FILE; HOWEVER, IT DOES NOT
  158                /       INCLUDE AN ORIGIN TO 0200 AS IS USUALLY THE CASE.  [AS SUCH, WERE IT AN ACTUAL
  159                /       TFS BINARY FILE, CERTAIN UTILITIES COULD REJECT IT AS INVALID.  SINCE IT IS
  160                /       ALWAYS THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0060, NO FILE SYSTEM ACCESS EXISTS.]
  161   
  162   07600* 7000          FL^4+OR^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA     /CONTROL WORD.
  163   
  164   07601* 6201          CDF     00                      /FIELD SETTING TO FIELD 0.
  165                        
  166   07602* 7757          SFILES                          /*SFILES
  167   
  168         *7757          RELOC   SFILES                  /WHERE THIS ASSEMBLES.
  169   
  170                /       WHEN CONTROL IS PASSED TO HERE, START THE BLOCK 0000 RELOADING PROCESS.
  171   
  172   07757* 1207  SLIGO,  TAD     SL600/(600)             /GET REWIND BITS.
  173   07760* 4213          JMS     SLWAIT                  /WAIT FOR THE TAPE TO REWIND.
  174   07761* 1223          TAD     SL7577/(SBOOT-1)        /SETUP THE
  175   07762* 3355          DCA     CA                      /CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER.
  176   
  177   07763* 0000          DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA     /CONTROL WORD.
  178   
  179         *7763          RELOC   .-1                     /RESET ASSEMBLY ADDRESS.
  180   
  181   07763* 1374          TAD     TRNLEN/(SBOOT-SADDR)    /GET WORD COUNT VALUE TO TRANSFER JUST
  182                                                        /ENOUGH OF THE SYSTEM HANDLER NEEDED.
  183   07764* 3354          DCA     WC                      /SETUP THE WORD COUNT REGISTER.
  184   07765* 1237          TAD     SL220/(220)             /GET READ FORWARD COMMAND BITS.
  185   07766* 6766          DTLA                            /START READING BLOCK 0000.
  186   07767* 6771          DTSF                            /FLAG UP?
  187   07770* 5367          JMP     .-1                     /NO, WAIT FOR IT.


/    SYSTEM HANDLER RELOAD ROUTINE   P?S PAL V08I    22-MAY-14  PAGE 5

  189   07771* 0000          DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA     /CONTROL WORD.
  190   
  191         *7771          RELOC   .-1                     /RESET ASSEMBLY ADDRESS.
  192   
  193                /       AT THIS POINT, [MOST OF] BLOCK 0000 IS READ IN.  WE CAN ACCESS CONSTANTS
  194                /       LOCATED WITHIN THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.
  195   
  196   07771* 1202          TAD     S200/(200)              /GET MOTION BIT.
  197   07772* 6764          DTXA                            /STOP THE TAPE.
  198   07773* 5346          JMP     SLUSTRT                 /GO START THE USER PROGRAM.
  199   
  200   07774* 7632  TRNLEN, SBOOT-SADDR                     /DESIRED TRANSFER LENGTH
  201   
  202   07775* 0000          ZBLOCK  1                       /EMPTY SPACE.
  203   
  204                /       THIS IS THE DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS OF A SAFE HALT.
  205   
  206   07776* 7402  DEFADR, HLT                             /DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS.
  207   
  208   07777* 1025          DA^4+OR^4+DA^4+EF^4+EF^4+EF     /CONTROL WORD.
  209   
  210         *7777          RELOC   .-1                     /RESET ASSEMBLY ADDRESS.
  211   
  212   07777* 5376          JMP     DEFADR                  /IN CASE THE USER RESTARTS THE MACHINE.
  213   
  214   00000* 7626          SLPSTRT                         /*SLPSTRT
  215   
  216         *7626          RELOC   SLPSTRT                 /WHERE THIS ASSEMBLES.
  217   
  218   07626* 5357          JMP     SLIGO                   /START OUR CODE AFTER WE'RE LOADED.
  219   
  220         *7231          RELOC                           /TURN OFF RELOCATION.
  221   
  222   07231  0000          ZBLOCK  .&7600+200-.            /EMPTY SPACE.
  223   
  224                        $                               /THAT'S ALL FOLK!


